/* 段落记忆 · 词层 5 · 子块 d：词头 → {tw:[关系词,关系类型], en, zh} */
window.APP_MERGE_NET(5,{"sub":"d","par":{"signify":{"tw":[["sign",4],["mean",2],["indicate",2],["accentuate",6],["significance",4],["emphasise",6],["significant",4]],"en":"At the annual health check, the doctor pointed to a small shadow on the scan and explained what it might signify. A single spot, she said, does not mean disease; many harmless marks carry the same sign. Still, she wanted to indicate the range of possibilities clearly, and she accentuated the few tests that would settle the question. I asked her to emphasise what I could change in daily life while we waited. She said sleep, walks, and less salt were significant for anyone my age, whatever the result showed. The full significance of the visit came later: three days of worry had taught me more about my habits than ten years of reminders. The second scan was clean, and I left the clinic with a strange new respect for ordinary days.","zh":"年度体检时，医生指着片子上的一小片阴影，解释它可能意味着什么。她说，单个斑点并不等于患病，许多无害的痕迹带着同样的征象。不过她想把各种可能性讲清楚，并着重强调那几项能一锤定音的检查。我请她趁等待的工夫，强调一下日常生活里我能改些什么。她说，无论结果如何，睡眠、散步和少盐对我这个年纪的人都很要紧。这次检查的全部意义是后来才显现的：三天担忧教会我的东西，胜过十年来的提醒。复查片子干净，我走出诊所时，对寻常日子多了一种奇怪的新的敬意。"},"temper":{"tw":[["temperance",4],["mood",0],["sulk",3],["change",2],["tantrum",6],["season",0],["peeve",3],["adjust",2],["anger",6],["humour",0]],"en":"During our summer trip the ferry was delayed four hours, and every kind of temper appeared on that dock. One man flew into open anger at the ticket desk, while a child nearby threw a small tantrum over an ice cream. My aunt, who prided herself on her humour, kept her mood light and tried to adjust everyone's plans with jokes. A young couple would sulk in turns, each peeve louder than the last, and an old sailor watched them with amusement. He said that in his season on the water he had learned one thing: rage never shortened a delay. A kind of temperance settled over the crowd as evening came, and the mood changed from complaint to shared picnic. When the ferry finally arrived, people almost regretted the wait.","zh":"夏天出行那回，渡船晚点了四个小时，码头上各种脾气都露了相。一个男人在售票口大发雷霆，旁边一个孩子为了冰淇淋闹起了小脾气。一向以风趣自居的姑妈始终心情明朗，用笑话帮大家调整计划。一对年轻情侣轮流生闷气，一个赌气比一个响，一位老水手饶有兴致地看着他们。他说自己常年跑船只悟出一个道理：发火从来缩短不了等待。傍晚来临，人群里升起一种自制与包容，气氛从抱怨变成了共享的野餐。渡船终于进港时，人们反倒有点舍不得这段等待。"},"shuffle":{"tw":[["mix",0],["cut",3],["walk",2],["tweak",6],["ruffle",0],["reshuffle",3],["transfer",2],["shake",6],["shamble",0]],"en":"At the table by the window, my aunt would shuffle the cards with a slow, careful motion. Her shuffle was never fast, but nobody could tell what she had dealt. She would cut the pack, mix the two halves, and then hand it to the next player. A young cousin would walk to the kitchen and come back with a shamble, dragging his feet on the boards. He liked to tweak the rules and ruffle the order of play whenever he lost. Once we had to reshuffle three times because a card fell under the chair. She would shake her head, transfer the deal to me, and start again, and the room grew quiet.","zh":"窗边那张桌子旁，我姑妈洗牌总是又慢又稳。她洗得从不快，可谁也猜不出她发了什么。她把牌切一下，两半一掺，再递给下家。一个小表弟会走到厨房去，回来时拖着脚，鞋底在木板上蹭。他一输就想改规矩，把出牌的次序搅乱。有一回一张牌掉到椅子底下，我们只好重洗了三遍。她摇摇头，把发牌的活儿交给我，从头再来。"},"slash":{"tw":[["cut",2],["cat",3],["beat",2],["reduce",6],["stroke",0],["switch",3],["land",2],["wage",6],["whip",3]],"en":"Every spring my uncle would slash the tall weeds along the fence before the sheep came out. He would cut a wide path with long strokes of the blade and beat down the dry stalks. A cat followed him through the grass and would switch its tail at every step. The council had decided to reduce the money for the lane, so he had to slash the wage he paid the boy who helped. His land was poor, and the work never seemed to end. Once he let the blade whip back and it took a thin line off his boot. He said a sharp edge is kinder than a dull one.","zh":"每年春天，羊群出来之前，我叔叔都要把篱笆边的高草砍掉。他挥着长刀，一下一下劈出宽宽一条路，把干枯的秆子打倒。一只猫跟着他在草里走，每走一步就甩一下尾巴。村里决定削减修那条小路的钱，他只好把帮工男孩的工钱也砍下去。他那块地薄，活儿好像永远干不完。有一回刀刃反弹回来，在他靴子上削出一道细口。他说，快刃比钝刃更仁慈。"},"smear":{"tw":[["spot",0],["blood",3],["charge",2],["discredit",6],["stain",0],["dust",3],["cover",2],["tactic",6],["blur",0]],"en":"While repairing the wall, the painter would smear a thin layer of paste over every crack. A dark spot of dust had to be covered before the new coat went on. He would work the paste with a flat knife and then blur the edge with his thumb. Once a red stain appeared on the ceiling, and he had to charge the owner for a second visit. A rival tried to discredit him with a story about the bill and to smear his name in the local paper. It was a cheap tactic, and the mark on his reputation faded in a month. A drop of blood on the cloth showed he had cut his hand.","zh":"补墙的时候，油漆匠会把一层薄薄的腻子抹在每道裂缝上。一块发黑的灰点得先盖住，才能刷新的漆。他用一把平刀把腻子抹开，再用拇指把边晕开。有一回天花板上渗出一片红渍，他只好又跑一趟，向房主另收了钱。一个同行编了个账单上的说法想坏他的名声，还在本地报纸上往他身上泼脏水。这手段很下作，他名声上的那道印子一个月就淡了。布上一点血，说明他的手被划破了。"},"sprinkle":{"tw":[["dust",0],["salt",3],["rain",2],["spoon",6],["scatter",0],["spray",3],["wet",2],["butter",6],["disperse",0]],"en":"Before the bread went in, my mother would sprinkle a little flour over the board. She would dust the tin with a soft brush and sprinkle salt into the dough with a spoon. A light rain outside would wet the window and make the kitchen feel warm. She liked to scatter seeds on top and then spray the crust with water. A knob of butter would melt on the hot loaf and disperse its smell through the house. She never let the flour fall too thick, or the crust would turn hard. The loaf had to rest for an hour before anyone touched it. We ate the first slice standing at the counter.","zh":"面包进炉之前，我母亲会在案板上撒一薄层面粉。她用软刷在模子里扑一层粉，再用勺子往面团里撒盐。外面下着小雨，把窗子打湿，厨房里显得格外暖。她喜欢在表面撒些籽，再往皮上喷点水。一小块黄油在热面包上化开，把香味散得满屋都是。她从不让人把面粉撒得太厚，不然皮会发硬。面包得搁一个钟头才能动。我们站在柜台边，把第一片吃了。"},"squash":{"tw":[["crush",0],["stamp",3],["press",2],["cup",6],["squeeze",0],["telescope",3],["vegetable",2],["barbecue",6],["mash",0]],"en":"In the back garden a single squash had grown so large that it took both hands to lift. My father would cut it into thick slices and mash the soft flesh with a fork. He liked to press a little salt into each piece before it went on the barbecue. The vegetable was heavy enough to crush the small plants beside it. He had to squeeze the seeds out, add a cup of water, and stamp the waste into the compost bin. Some summers the vines would telescope across the path and leave no room to walk. We ate squash for a week, and the kitchen smelled of smoke and sugar.","zh":"后园里一只南瓜长得太大，得两只手才抬得动。我父亲把它切成厚片，用叉子把软肉捣成泥。他喜欢在每片上按一点盐，再放上烤架。这东西沉得能把旁边的小苗压坏。他得把籽挤出来，加一杯水，再把渣踩进堆肥桶里。有些夏天藤蔓会一路伸过小路，连走的地方都不留。我们吃了一个星期的南瓜，厨房里满是烟和糖的味道。"},"stalk":{"tw":[["stem",0],["branch",3],["hunt",2],["leaf",6],["haunt",0],["stock",3],["walk",2],["chop",6],["straw",0]],"en":"A tall stalk of corn stood alone at the edge of the field, taller than any branch of the old tree behind it. My cousin would cut it at the stem and strip every leaf for the animals. He had to chop the dry straw into short pieces and store it in the stock shed. In the evening he would walk the field to hunt for rabbits that came to feed. A grey fox would haunt the same corner every night, and he never took it. He said the fox had more right to the stalk than we did. Nobody in the family could walk past that field without looking.","zh":"田边孤零零立着一株高玉米，比后面那棵老树任何一根枝子都高。我表哥会从茎部把它砍下，把叶子一片片剥下来喂牲口。他得把干秸秆剁成短段，存进放草料的棚子。傍晚他会在地里走一圈，找那些来吃食的兔子。一只灰狐每天夜里都守在同一角，他从来没动过它。他说，那株玉米狐比我们更有份。家里没有人走过那块地时不往那边看一眼。"},"sway":{"tw":[["carry",0],["roll",3],["move",2],["clout",6],["rock",0],["lash",3],["power",2],["exert",6],["shake",0]],"en":"In the village meeting, the old teacher still had a quiet sway over every decision. She would carry the room with a few plain words and never raise her voice. People said her clout came from years of fair dealing rather than from any office. Her power lay in small things: she would roll up her sleeves, listen, and then speak. She could rock a stubborn argument without ever losing her temper. Once a storm began to lash the windows, and she had to exert herself to be heard above it. The chairman would shake his head, but he always let her have the last word. In the end the vote went her way, and the room began to move toward the door.","zh":"村里的会上，那位老教师对每个决定仍有一种不声张的影响力。她几句话就能带动全场，从不提高嗓门。人们说她的分量来自多年公道做事，而不是哪个职位。她的力量都在小处：挽起袖子，听人说完，然后开口。她能把一场僵住的争论晃松动，自己却从不上火。有一回风暴开始抽打窗户，她只好使劲把话送出去。主席会摇头，可最后总是让她说最后一句。结果投票按她的意思过了，屋里的人开始往门口挪。"},"tack":{"tw":[["piece",0],["bit",3],["join",2],["jab",6],["flip",0],["line",2],["skirt",6],["sheet",0]],"en":"On Saturday I decided to repair the old notice board in the kitchen. I spread a clean sheet on the table and sorted the tools piece by piece, keeping every small bit in a shallow dish. The first tack went in easily, but the second bent when I gave it a hard jab with the hammer. I had to flip the board over and join the two broken halves with a thin strip of wood. A line of tiny holes showed where the old nails had been, so I skirted those spots and started again. By evening the board hung straight on the wall, and it has not moved since.","zh":"周六我决定修好厨房里那块旧告示板。我在桌上铺开一张干净的布，把工具一件件分好，每个小零件都放在浅盘里。第一枚平头钉很顺利地钉了进去，可我用锤子重重一敲时，第二枚就弯了。我只好把板子翻过来，用一条薄木片把裂开的两半接上。一排细小的孔说明旧钉子原来钉在哪里，我便绕开这些地方重新开始。到傍晚，板子已经端端正正挂在墙上，再没动过。"},"thump":{"tw":[["beat",0],["flap",3],["blow",2],["shriek",6],["pound",0],["thrash",3],["hit",2],["growl",6],["poke",0]],"en":"All night the wind kept up a steady thump against the kitchen door. A loose branch would beat the glass, then flap and go silent, then hit again with a heavier blow. Somewhere above us a metal sheet began to shriek, and the rain seemed to pound the roof in long waves. Our old dog would growl at each new sound and then thrash about on his blanket. I lay awake and gave my brother a poke in the back whenever he started to snore. By two in the morning the whole frame of the house seemed to shake with it. At dawn the storm had gone, leaving only a soft drip and one bent gutter.","zh":"一整夜，风都在厨房门上撞出沉闷的响声。一根松脱的树枝拍打玻璃，扑腾几下又安静下来，然后更重地再撞一次。头顶某处一块铁皮开始尖啸，雨也像一波波地砸在屋顶上。我们那条老狗每听到一个新声音就低吼，然后在毯子上翻来覆去。我躺着没睡着，弟弟一打呼噜我就用手指戳他后背。到凌晨两点，整座房子的框架似乎都跟着震动。到早晨暴风雨过去了，只剩下轻轻的滴水声和一道弯掉的檐槽。"},"torment":{"tw":[["frustrate",0],["tease",3],["pain",2],["endure",6],["agony",0],["martyr",3],["injure",2],["despair",6],["curse",0]],"en":"For three winters my sister had to endure a dull pain in her right knee. The injury was small, but it could frustrate her for weeks, and the quiet torment of it showed in the way she walked. Some mornings the agony was bad enough to keep her in bed. She would not complain, though she sometimes played the martyr in a way that made the rest of us feel guilty. Doctors could not agree on a cure, and one warned that another fall might injure the joint for good. There were days of real despair, when she would curse the stairs in our building. What finally helped was slow exercise, not the pills she used to tease me about.","zh":"连着三个冬天，姐姐都得忍受右膝那种闷闷的疼。伤势并不重，却能让她烦躁好几个星期，而这份默默的折磨从她走路的姿势里就看得出来。有些早晨痛得厉害，她只能待在床上。她从不抱怨，只是偶尔把自己扮成受难者，弄得我们其他人都觉得内疚。医生们对怎么治意见不一，其中一个还警告说再摔一次可能就把关节弄坏了。也有真正绝望的日子，那时她会咒骂我们楼里的楼梯。最后起作用的是慢慢锻炼，而不是她常拿来打趣我的那些药片。"},"trench":{"tw":[["deep",0],["furrow",3],["cut",2],["skirt",6],["ditch",0],["moat",3],["dig",2],["brush",6],["entrench",0]],"en":"Behind the garden wall there is a deep trench that carries rain away from the house. Last spring my father decided to dig it out again, because the old ditch had filled with leaves. He cut a straight furrow along the path, then skirted the apple tree so the roots would not be damaged. I helped with a stiff brush, clearing mud from the stones, while he stood in the trench and threw the soil up in slow loads. Beyond the hedge, the dry moat of the old castle was already green with weeds. Since then he has been entrenched in the idea that the garden must be dug again every year.","zh":"花园围墙后面有一条很深的沟渠，把雨水引离房子。去年春天父亲决定再把它挖一遍，因为旧沟里已经塞满了落叶。他沿小路切出一道笔直的沟痕，又绕开苹果树，免得伤到树根。我拿一把硬毛刷帮忙刷掉石头上的泥，他则站在沟里，一铲一铲慢慢把土抛上来。树篱那边，古堡干涸的护城河早已长满青草。从那以后他就固守一个念头：这园子每年都得重挖一次。"},"twitch":{"tw":[["flip",0],["move",2],["sinew",6],["squeeze",0],["tweak",3],["pull",2],["hum",6],["jerk",0]],"en":"The physiotherapist asked me to sit still while she watched the muscle above my knee twitch. Every small jerk told her which sinew was still weak, and she would gently tweak my ankle to see how it answered. I tried not to move when she gave my calf a firm squeeze, though the pull of it made me flinch. Between sets she would hum an old tune, which made the whole hour easier. At the end she told me to flip a small weight from hand to hand, ten times on each side. It looked simple, but my arm was shaking by the fourth round. She wrote a note on a chart and said the progress was normal.","zh":"理疗师让我坐着别动，她则盯着我膝盖上方那块肌肉的抽动。每一次细微的急跳都告诉她哪条肌腱还很弱，她会轻轻拧一下我的脚踝，看它怎么反应。她用力捏我的小腿时，我努力不动，可那股牵扯还是让我缩了一下。每组之间她会哼一首老调子，让整个小时轻松了不少。结束时她让我把一个小重物在两手之间翻来翻去，每边十次。看着简单，可我做到第四轮手臂就在抖了。她在表格上记了一笔，说恢复情况正常。"},"veto":{"tw":[["negative",0],["bar",3],["power",2],["approve",6],["prohibit",0],["kill",3],["command",2],["repeal",6],["forbid",0]],"en":"The committee met on Thursday to decide whether to approve the new shift plan. The manager had the power to veto it, and for a while it looked as if she would. Two members gave a firm negative before anyone had even read the figures. The rules prohibit any change that would cut rest time, and our union contract can bar a plan that skips the safety check. She did not kill the idea outright, but she did command a second review. In the end we agreed to change one clause, and she promised to repeal the oldest rule rather than block everything. Nobody dared forbid a further meeting, and the plan went back to the staff for comments.","zh":"委员会周四开会，决定是否批准新的排班方案。经理有权否决它，有一阵子看样子她真要这么做。还没人读完数据，就有两位成员明确表示反对。规定禁止任何削减休息时间的改动，我们的工会合同也能挡住跳过安全检查的方案。她并没有一下子把想法掐死，而是要求再复核一次。最后我们同意改掉一条条款，她也答应废除那条最老的规则，而不是把一切都封死。没人敢说以后不许再开会，方案被退回去征求员工意见。"},"wedge":{"tw":[["force",0],["impact",3],["move",2],["bunker",6],["stick",0],["compress",3],["block",2],["hole",6],["deposit",0]],"en":"At the old bunker museum, the guide showed us a steel door that had been stuck for years. Someone had driven a wedge into the frame, and the marks of that impact are still visible on the wall. Two men used to push with all their force, but the door would not move. In the end they had to compress a strip of lead and stick it under the hinge, then block the gap with a stone. A small hole in the concrete let in a thin line of light, and dust formed a pale deposit on the floor. The guide said visitors still try to shift the wedge with their hands.","zh":"在那座旧掩体博物馆里，向导给我们看一扇卡了很多年的钢门。有人把一只楔子打进过门框，撞击留下的痕迹还在墙上。从前两个人用尽全力推，门也纹丝不动。最后他们只好把一条铅压扁，塞到铰链下面，再用一块石头把缝隙堵住。混凝土上的一个小孔透进一线光，灰尘在地面落成薄薄一层。向导说，如今还有游客用手去掰那只楔子。"},"wink":{"tw":[["flash",0],["bat",3],["moment",2],["smirk",6],["instant",0],["flicker",3],["radiate",2],["chuckle",6],["blink",0]],"en":"My grandmother hates having her photo taken, so the whole thing usually takes a while. The camera gave a bright flash, and in that instant she closed her eyes and gave a small blink. My uncle made a joke, and she answered with a quick wink and a smirk that told us she was enjoying herself. For a moment nobody moved; then the light began to flicker and the bulb died. She did not bat an eye, she just told us to use the phone instead. In the end the best picture shows her laughing, her face seeming to radiate warmth, while we can hear my uncle's low chuckle behind the camera.","zh":"外婆讨厌拍照，所以每次都要折腾好一阵。相机闪了一下强光，就在那一瞬间她闭上眼，轻轻眨了一下。舅舅讲了个笑话，她回了个飞快的眼色和一抹得意的笑，说明她其实挺享受。有一刻谁都没动，接着灯光开始闪，灯泡灭了。她连眼皮都没眨一下，只叫我们改用手机拍。最后最好的一张是她大笑的样子，脸上像在发着暖意，而我们还能听见镜头后舅舅低低的笑声。"},"witch":{"tw":[["glamour",0],["spell",3],["charm",2],["enchant",0],["voodoo",3],["pagan",2],["evil",6],["bewitch",0]],"en":"For the school play my cousin had to dress as a witch, and she took the part very seriously. Her costume had a cheap glamour about it: a black hat, a silver charm on a chain, and a cloak that shimmered under the lights. In one scene she had to recite a spell over a paper cauldron, and the audience gasped as if she could truly enchant them. The story was an old pagan tale about a village that feared evil and blamed a lonely woman for every bad harvest. By the last act she had managed to bewitch the whole hall, and even the teachers clapped. Someone joked that she had used voodoo on the judges.","zh":"学校演出时表妹要扮成女巫，她把这个角色看得很认真。她的戏服有一种廉价而迷人的味道：一顶黑帽、链子上挂着一枚银饰，还有一件在灯下泛光的斗篷。有一场她要对着纸做的锅念咒，观众倒吸一口气，仿佛她真能把人迷住。故事是个古老的异教传说，说一个村子害怕邪恶，把每一次歉收都怪在一个孤独的女人身上。到最后一幕，她真把整个礼堂都镇住了，连老师都鼓掌。有人开玩笑说她对评委施了巫术。"},"zip":{"tw":[["hurry",0],["run",3],["force",2],["overlay",6],["zero",0],["zoom",3],["travel",2],["pocket",6],["energy",0]],"en":"The courier had to hurry because the shop closed at six. He ran up four flights with the parcel, then had to force the zip on his bag, which had caught on a loose thread. His phone showed a map overlay in bright green, and the dot of his route would zoom in whenever he turned a corner. By the time he reached the door his energy was almost at zero. He took the receipt from his pocket and asked me to sign, then said he still had to travel across the city for one more delivery. I told him to take the lift down, and he laughed. I offered him a glass of water, but he was already at the stairs.","zh":"快递员得赶紧，因为店六点就关门。他抱着包裹跑上四层楼，然后还得使劲拉上背包的拉链，那拉链卡在一根松线上。他的手机上是亮绿色的地图叠层，每次拐弯，路线的那个小点就会放大。等他到门口时，体力几乎已经归零。他从口袋里掏出签收单让我签字，然后说他还得穿过整座城去送下一件。我叫他坐电梯下去，他笑了。我请他喝杯水，可他已经走到楼梯口了。"},"skeleton":{"tw":[["skeletal",4],["frame",0],["hoop",3],["system",2],["vault",6],["minimum",2],["body",6]],"en":"In the old hall of the museum hangs the skeleton of a huge sea animal. Its long frame is held together by thin wires, and each rib curves like a hoop above the stone floor. A guide explained how the skeletal structure supports a body that once weighed as much as a small truck. Above us the vault of the ceiling was painted with faded stars, which made the whole room feel like a cave. The museum keeps the lighting at a minimum to protect the bones. The system that holds the display in place was rebuilt only two years ago. Children stood in a quiet ring below it, and nobody spoke for a while.","zh":"博物馆的旧展厅里悬着一具巨大海洋动物的骨架。它长长的骨架用细钢丝连在一起，每一根肋骨都像铁箍一样拱在石地上方。一位讲解员解释了这套骨骼结构如何支撑起一具曾重达一辆小卡车的身躯。我们头顶的拱顶画着褪色的星星，让整个厅像个洞穴。博物馆把灯光压到最低限度，以保护这些骨头。固定展品的那个系统两年前才重建过。"},"therapeutic":{"tw":[["therapy",4],["cure",0],["acoustic",3],["efficacy",6],["remedy",0],["panacea",3],["prenatal",6]],"en":"At the clinic my mother joined a small group that uses music as a form of therapy. A nurse with an acoustic guitar leads the session, and the aim is not to cure anything but to lessen pain and worry. Nobody claims it is a panacea, yet the staff keep records of its efficacy, and the numbers are quietly encouraging. For my mother, the best remedy turned out to be simple: an hour a week of singing with strangers. The programme began as a prenatal class for expectant mothers and slowly opened to everyone. She says she sleeps better on the nights she goes. She describes the hour as therapeutic rather than medical, and the nurses agree.","zh":"在诊所里，母亲加入了一个把音乐当作治疗方式的小组。一位护士抱着木吉他带大家唱，目的不是治好什么病，而是减轻疼痛和忧虑。没人说这是万能灵药，但工作人员会记录它的效果，数据令人悄悄振奋。对母亲来说，最好的疗法其实很简单：每周和一屋子陌生人唱一个小时。这个项目最初是给准妈妈的产前课程，后来慢慢对所有人开放。她说去唱歌的那些晚上睡得更香。"},"transit":{"tw":[["transition",4],["passage",0],["cut",3],["bring",2],["rail",6],["pass",2],["metro",6]],"en":"Our journey home involved three changes and a long transit through a crowded station. The passage between the two platforms was narrow, and people with heavy bags had to pass each other slowly. We took the metro first, then a rail line that cut across the northern hills. The transition from the warm carriage to the cold street took us by surprise. A porter helped bring our cases up the stairs, and I gave him the last of my coins. By the time we reached the bus stop, the sky had turned the colour of wet slate. We had bought the tickets weeks before, but the times had changed twice on the board.","zh":"我们回家的路上换了三次车，还在拥挤的车站里走了很长一段。两个月台之间的通道很窄，提着大包的人只能慢慢相互让过。我们先坐地铁，然后换了一条横穿北部丘陵的铁路线。从暖和的车厢一下到寒冷的街上，我们都有点措手不及。一位搬运工帮我们把箱子提上台阶，我把最后几枚硬币给了他。等走到公交站时，天色已经暗成湿石板那样的灰。"},"saddle":{"tw":[["charge",0],["overwhelm",3],["cut",2],["pony",6],["burden",0],["overburden",3],["pass",2],["hump",6]],"en":"On the second day of our mountain trek, the guide tightened the saddle on a small brown pony and told me to keep my weight forward on the climbs. The animal carried a heavy burden of bags, and I worried that we were overburdening it. He laughed and said the pony had carried worse loads up worse hills, and that I should not let worry overwhelm me. We cut across a stream, passed a line of pines, and started up a long hump of rock that took an hour to cross. Halfway up, the pony stopped and refused to charge forward until the guide spoke to it quietly. I paid a small charge at the top hut for water and rest, and we rode down before the light went.","zh":"进山徒步的第二天，向导在一匹棕色小马背上把马鞍勒紧，让我上坡时把重心往前压。那牲口驮着一大堆行李，我担心我们让它负担过重了。他笑说这匹马驮过更重的东西、爬过更陡的坡，让我别让担心把自己压垮。我们横穿一条溪，经过一排松树，开始爬一道要走一小时才能翻过去的长石脊。爬到一半，马停住不肯往前冲，直到向导轻声跟它说话。我在山顶小屋付了一点钱买水和休息，趁天没黑就下山了。"},"scoop":{"tw":[["best",0],["dip",3],["beat",2],["spoon",6],["pocket",0],["report",2],["puff",6],["exclusive",0]],"en":"On my first week at the local paper, the editor gave me a tip that turned into an exclusive. A worker at the old ice factory had found a crack in the roof, and the company had kept it quiet for months. The temperature had dipped below zero, so I put a spoon from the canteen, a notebook, and a small camera in my pocket and went to see for myself. It took two hours to beat the guard at the gate, and in the end I simply asked him to let me in. The report ran on Friday, with a photograph of a scoop of ice on the floor and a puff of steam above it. It was not the best story of the year, but it was the first one with my name on it, and I still keep a copy.","zh":"进本地报社的第一周，编辑给了我一条线索，后来成了独家新闻。老冰厂的一名工人发现屋顶有裂缝，公司却瞒了几个月。那天温度降到零下，我把食堂的一把勺子、一个本子和兜里的小相机带上，自己去看。我在门口跟门卫周旋了两个小时，最后还是直接请他放我进去。报道周五见报，配了一张地上那勺冰、上方一缕蒸汽的照片。那不是全年最好的稿子，却是第一篇署我名字的，我到现在还留着。"},"smack":{"tw":[["smell",0],["blow",2],["gutter",6],["taste",0],["hit",2],["spit",6],["bang",0]],"en":"The storm hit just as I reached the market, and the first smack of rain on the metal awning sounded like applause. Within a minute water ran down the gutter and the smell of wet stone rose from the pavement. A sudden blow of wind turned two umbrellas inside out, and the bang of a shutter made everyone duck. I could taste dust and rain together, a strange mix that I somehow liked. A man near the fish stall began to spit out the water that had run into his mouth, and a boy laughed so hard he had to sit down. Then the rain stopped as quickly as it had come, and the whole street steamed in the sun. I walked home slowly, my shoes full of water and my ears still ringing.","zh":"我刚走到市场，暴风雨就来了，第一阵雨点拍在铁皮雨棚上的声响像一片掌声。不到一分钟，水就顺着排水沟往下淌，湿石头的味道从路面升起来。一阵突来的风把两把伞吹翻了，卷帘门的一声巨响让所有人都缩了一下。我能尝到灰尘和雨水混在一起的味道，奇怪的是我竟有点喜欢。鱼摊旁边一个男人开始把流进嘴里的水吐出来，一个男孩笑得不得不坐下。然后雨说停就停，整条街在太阳下冒起热气。我慢慢走回家，鞋里全是水，耳朵还在嗡嗡响。"},"soothe":{"tw":[["comfort",0],["calm",3],["relieve",2],["irritate",1],["assuage",6],["console",0],["allay",6],["solace",0]],"en":"When my son had a fever last winter, the only thing that seemed to soothe him was a warm cloth on his forehead. I would sit by his bed, comfort him with a quiet story, and try to calm my own voice so that he would not hear my worry. The medicine relieved the fever for a few hours, but the cough would return and irritate him until he cried. I learned to console him with small promises: a glass of water, a song, one more minute of light. No word could allay his fear of the dark, and only a hand on his back seemed to assuage it. In the morning he was better, and I found some solace in the fact that he had slept at last. I never told him how frightened I had been.","zh":"去年冬天儿子发烧，唯一能让他安静下来的，是额头上的一块温毛巾。我坐在他床边，用轻声的故事安慰他，也压住自己的嗓音，好让他听不出我的担心。药能让烧退几个小时，可咳嗽总会回来，弄得他烦躁到哭。我学会用小小的承诺哄他：一杯水、一首歌、再多一分钟的灯。什么话都平息不了他对黑的害怕，只有一只手放在他背上似乎能缓解。早上他好了些，我因为他终于睡着了而得到一点慰藉。我从没告诉他我当时有多怕。"},"sorrow":{"tw":[["regret",0],["mourn",3],["suffer",2],["joy",1],["anguish",6],["grief",3],["remorse",6],["grieve",0]],"en":"When our old dog died in the spring, the whole house filled with a quiet sorrow that nobody knew how to name. My mother would mourn him in small ways, setting his bowl down before she remembered, then standing still with regret on her face. My brother suffered in silence and would not talk about it at all. I felt a sharp anguish the first night, and then a softer grief that lasted for weeks. There was no remorse in any of us, because we had given him a good life, and that knowledge was a strange comfort. We grieve slowly, my father said, because we loved slowly and for a long time. By summer we could remember him with joy, and we planted a small tree where he used to sleep.","zh":"春天老狗死的那天，整座房子都充满一种谁也说不清的、安静的悲伤。母亲会用一些细小的方式哀悼他：把他的碗放下才想起，然后带着懊悔站在那里。弟弟默默地承受，一个字也不肯说。第一晚我感到一阵尖锐的痛苦，之后是一种更柔软的哀伤，持续了好几周。我们谁都没有愧疚，因为我们给过他好日子，这份明白是一种奇怪的安慰。父亲说，我们哀伤得慢，是因为我们爱得慢、爱得久。到了夏天，我们已经能带着欢喜想起他，还在他常睡的地方种了一棵小树。"},"sour":{"tw":[["dark",0],["taste",2],["sweet",1],["yogurt",6],["work",0],["cocktail",2],["fresh",6],["ferment",0]],"en":"I left a bowl of milk on the warm shelf for two days to let it ferment, and by Sunday it had turned into a thick, sour yogurt. The taste was sharper than the one from the shop, and I liked it with honey and a little fruit. My first attempt had gone wrong: the milk was not fresh, and the result was a thin liquid with a dark skin on top. This time I kept the jar away from light and let the culture work at its own speed. I used the yogurt in a cold cocktail with lime and ice, which sounded strange but tasted sweet and clean. My brother watched me drink it and said the kitchen smelled like a brewery. He was not far wrong.","zh":"我把一碗牛奶放在温暖的架子上两天，让它发酵，到周日它就变成了浓稠的酸酸奶。味道比店里买的更尖锐，我喜欢加蜂蜜和一点水果。第一次做失败了：牛奶不新鲜，结果是稀薄的液体，上面浮着一层暗色的皮。这回我把罐子放在避光处，让菌种按自己的速度工作。我用这酸奶调了一杯加青柠和冰的冷饮，听着奇怪，喝起来却又甜又干净。弟弟看我喝，说厨房闻起来像酿酒厂。他离真相不远。"},"spite":{"tw":[["hurt",0],["humiliate",3],["arouse",2],["lack",6],["injure",0],["sting",3],["despite",6],["wound",0]],"en":"A colleague once spread a small rumour about me, not out of any real malice but out of pure spite over a promotion she had lost. She would make a quiet remark in meetings, just enough to arouse doubt about my work, and then smile as if nothing had happened. It did not injure my career, but the words still sting when I think of them, and I felt the lack of any honest conversation more than the insult itself. I decided not to answer in the same way, despite the temptation to humiliate her in front of the team. Instead I asked her to help with a project, which seemed to wound her pride more than any reply. Months later she apologized, and I realized that hurt people often speak in spite.","zh":"有位同事曾散布过关于我的一个小谣言，不是出于什么真正的恶意，纯粹是因为她没得到那次升职的怨气。她会在会上轻声说一句，刚好够让人对我的工作生出怀疑，然后像什么都没发生一样微笑。这并没有损害我的事业，但那些话至今想起来还刺人，比起那句侮辱，我更感到缺少一次坦诚的谈话。尽管很想当众让她难堪，我还是决定不用同样的方式回击。我反而请她帮忙做一个项目，这似乎比任何回话都更伤她的自尊。几个月后她道了歉，我才明白，受伤的人常常是用怨气说话的。"},"stool":{"tw":[["pot",0],["dung",3],["grow",2],["urine",6],["toilet",0],["seat",2],["swab",6],["tiller",0]],"en":"The nurse who visits our village once a month set up her table in the barn, beside a wooden stool and a shelf of glass pots. She asked my uncle for a stool sample and a urine sample, and she took a swab from his throat with a thin stick. He joked that the only thing he had ever given a doctor before was a basket of eggs. While she wrote, he told her about the dung he spreads on the fields to help the crop grow, and about the old tiller he repairs every spring. She said the toilet in the yard should be moved further from the well, and he promised to do it before the rains. Then he sat on the seat of his tractor and drove us both home.","zh":"每月来我们村一次的护士把桌子架在谷仓里，旁边是一条木凳和一架玻璃罐。她让我叔叔留一份大便样本和一份尿样，又用一根细棍在他喉咙里取了拭子。他开玩笑说，他这辈子给医生的只有一篮鸡蛋。她写记录的时候，他跟她讲起撒在田里帮庄稼生长的粪肥，还有他每年春天都要修的那台旧耕地机。她说院子里的厕所该挪得离井远一些，他答应雨季前就办。然后他坐上拖拉机的座位，把我们俩都载回了家。"},"stump":{"tw":[["stamp",0],["stool",3],["clear",2],["finger",6],["pulpit",0],["post",2],["dole",6],["podium",0]],"en":"The village meeting was held in a field where an old tree had been cut down, and the speaker used the stump as his podium. He was a thin man who had been on the dole for two years, and he spoke with the confidence of a preacher in a pulpit. His argument was simple: the council should clear the fallen wood, post a notice, and let the young families use the land. Someone asked him to stamp the plan with an official mark, and he laughed and said he had no stamp, only a finger and a promise. He stood on a wooden stool to be seen above the crowd, then stepped down carefully. By sunset the stump was gone and the first post of a fence was in the ground.","zh":"村民大会就在一棵老树被砍倒的地里开，讲话的人把树桩当成了他的讲台。他是个瘦瘦的男人，领了两年失业救济，说起话来却像布道坛上的牧师一样有底气。他的道理很简单：镇里该把倒下的木头清走，贴一张告示，让有小孩的年轻家庭用这块地。有人让他给方案盖个公章，他笑说自己没有章，只有一根手指和一句承诺。他站到一条木凳上让大家都能看见，然后小心地下来。太阳落山前，树桩已经不见了，篱笆的第一根柱子也立进了土里。"},"swap":{"tw":[["switch",0],["thrash",3],["travel",2],["negotiate",6],["trade",0],["exchange",2],["deal",6],["barter",0]],"en":"Every autumn our town holds a swap meet in the school hall, where people bring things they no longer want and trade them for something else. Last year I took an old lamp and a box of tools, and I came home with a bicycle bell and a wooden box. The rules are simple: no money changes hands, and everyone has to negotiate every exchange face to face. I watched two men barter over a fishing rod for twenty minutes before they finally made a deal. A boy tried to swap his football for a pair of skates, then decided to switch to a comic instead. Nobody seemed to lose, and nobody tried to thrash out a better price at the end. The whole afternoon felt like travel to another, slower economy.","zh":"每年秋天我们镇都在学校礼堂办一场旧物交换会，人们把不再需要的东西拿来，换点别的。去年我带去一盏旧灯和一箱工具，回家时多了一个自行车铃和一个木盒。规矩很简单：不用钱，每一次交换都得当面谈成。我看着两个男人为一根钓竿讨价还价了二十分钟，最后才成交。一个男孩想用足球换一双溜冰鞋，后来又改主意换了一本漫画。好像没人吃亏，最后也没人再想争个更好的价钱。整个下午像是去了一趟另一个节奏更慢的经济体。"},"tailor":{"tw":[["cut",0],["quilt",3],["adapt",2],["fancy",6],["sew",0],["design",2],["smart",6],["orient",0]],"en":"The tailor on our street learned his trade from his father, and he still cuts every pattern by hand on a long wooden table. Last winter I brought him my grandfather's coat, which was too big across the shoulders, and asked whether he could adapt it. He looked at the seams, drew a line with chalk, and said the design was worth saving. He had to sew a new lining and replace a panel with cloth from an old quilt he kept in a drawer. While he worked, he talked about the fancy shops in the city that send their suits to him for repair. He said a smart coat should be oriented to the body, not to the season. When I put it on, it fitted as if it had always been mine.","zh":"我们街上的那位裁缝是从父亲那里学的手艺，至今仍在一条长木桌上手工裁每一个版型。去年冬天我把祖父的大衣拿给他，肩太宽了，问他能不能改。他看了看缝线，用粉笔画了一道线，说这个版型值得救。他得缝一层新衬里，再用他抽屉里一床旧被子上的布补上一块。干活时他聊起城里那些讲究的店，把西装送到他这里来修。他说一件挺括的大衣该顺着身体来定，而不是顺着季节。我穿上时，它合得像本来就是我的。"},"trickle":{"tw":[["filter",0],["leach",3],["run",2],["swell",6],["drip",0],["flow",2],["evaporate",6],["dribble",0]],"en":"The spring behind our garden had slowed to a trickle by midsummer, so my father built a small stone basin to catch it. Water would drip from the rock all night, and by morning a thin flow ran along the channel we had dug. We laid a cloth filter of sand and gravel so the soil would not leach into the pool. On hot afternoons the stream would shrink, and half of it seemed to evaporate before it reached the beans. When rain finally came, the little channel began to swell, and water would dribble over the edge and soak the path. My father laughed and said a garden teaches patience: what trickles today may flow tomorrow. By August the basin was full, and the beans stood taller than my knee.","zh":"到了仲夏，我们花园后面的泉水已经细成一股涓流，父亲便砌了个小石池把它蓄住。水整夜从岩石上滴下来，天亮时已沿着我们挖的小沟缓缓流淌。我们铺了一层沙石做的滤层，免得泥土渗进池里。炎热的下午水流会变小，有一半还没流到豆子地里就好像蒸发了。等雨终于来了，小水沟开始涨起来，水从边沿溢出去，把小路泡得透湿。父亲笑着说，种园子教人耐心：今天只是滴答的水，明天也许就能流成一条。到八月池子满了，豆子长得比我的膝盖还高。"},"triple":{"tw":[["trio",0],["trilogy",3],["hit",2],["double",6],["treble",0],["multiple",5],["quadruple",6],["triad",0]],"en":"Our neighbour's band spent two years on a project that grew into a triple album, three records sold as one heavy box. The trio had started in a garage with a single hit that local radio played all summer. Their first record was a double set, and the second grew into a trilogy about the river near their town. By the end the price had trebled, and the box came with multiple booklets and a folded poster. A fourth player joined for one tour, so for a few weeks they joked about becoming a quadruple act. The three of them still called themselves a triad of friends first and a band second. When the box finally arrived, we played all six sides in one evening.","zh":"邻居的乐队花了两年做一张三张一套的专辑，三张唱片装在一个很沉的盒子里卖。这个三人组合最初是在车库里起家的，一首单曲被本地电台播了一整个夏天。第一张唱片是双张，第二张发展成了关于城边那条河的三部曲。到最后价格涨了三倍，盒子里还附了好几本小册子和一张折叠海报。巡演时多了一位第四位乐手，有那么几周他们开玩笑说自己成了四重组合。可这三个人始终说，他们先是三个人的朋友，然后才是一支乐队。盒子终于寄到那天，我们一个晚上把六面全听完了。"},"vest":{"tw":[["invest",0],["crown",3],["dress",2],["jacket",6],["robe",0],["ordain",3],["install",2],["camouflage",6]],"en":"Every autumn our village holds a small ceremony to install a new keeper of the old orchard. The chosen neighbour is dressed in a plain vest sewn by her grandmother, and over it she wears a green robe that still smells of cedar. The elders crown her with a wreath of dried leaves and ordain her with a few quiet words about patience. They invest her with one key and one ledger, and the whole square claps. Her brother stands at the back in an army jacket with a faded camouflage pattern, which looks odd beside all the clean linen. Afterwards we walk to the trees, and she puts on an old vest again to climb a ladder. By dusk the new keeper has already picked her first basket.","zh":"每年秋天，我们村子都会举行一个小仪式，为老果园迎立一位新的看园人。被选中的邻居穿着一件她祖母缝的素色背心，外面罩着一件还带着雪松味的绿色长袍。长辈们给她戴上干叶编的花冠，用几句关于耐心的话为她祝圣。他们把一把钥匙和一本账册交到她手里，整个广场都鼓起掌来。她弟弟站在后面，穿着一件迷彩已经褪色的军装夹克，在一屋子素净的亚麻衣服里显得有点怪。仪式结束后我们走向果树，她又换上那件旧背心去爬梯子。天还没黑，这位新看园人已经摘下了第一篮果子。"},"void":{"tw":[["empty",5],["break",3],["change",2],["absolute",6],["vacuum",0],["space",2],["clause",6],["vacancy",0]],"en":"The day we handed back the flat, the rooms looked strangely empty, and the hallway opened into a void where the bookcase had stood. My sister stayed in that space for a while, listening to the absolute quiet. We had signed a clause promising to leave no marks, so we filled every hole and cleaned the carpet with a vacuum. The landlord said the vacancy would be easy to fill, since the street was popular with students. Leaving felt like a small break in a life that had been steady for years. Change is always like that: a door closes, and for a week you walk through a void. Then the new flat begins to feel like a place, and the old one becomes a story.","zh":"交还房子那天，房间空得有些古怪，走廊在原来放书架的地方敞开成一片空白。姐姐在那块空地上站了一会儿，听着那种彻底的安静。我们签过一条条款，保证不在墙上留痕迹，于是把每个钉孔都补上，还用吸尘器清了地毯。房东说这房子不难租出去，因为这条街很受学生欢迎。搬走像是生活里一个小小的断裂，而这样的生活已经稳定了好多年。变化总是这样：一扇门关上，接下来一个星期你都走在一片空荡里。然后新房子慢慢像个地方了，旧房子则成了一段故事。"},"wrestle":{"tw":[["twist",0],["wrench",3],["move",2],["steer",6],["worm",0],["battle",2],["confine",6],["grapple",0]],"en":"Getting the old sofa up to the third floor was a battle we nearly lost. The stair was narrow, and the frame would not bend, so we had to twist it and wrench it around the corner while my uncle steered from below. For ten minutes we could only grapple with the same wooden arm, sweating and laughing at the same time. The walls seemed to confine us to a space no wider than the sofa itself. At last my cousin wormed his way under the base and pushed while I pulled, and the thing slid up like a tired animal. We had to wrestle it through the last door before it would move at all. When it finally stood in the living room, we sat on it and said nothing.","zh":"把那张旧沙发抬到三楼，是一场我们差点输掉的硬仗。楼梯很窄，沙发框架又不会弯，我们只好一边扭一边硬掰着转过拐角，叔叔在下面帮着调整方向。有十分钟我们只能跟同一条木扶手较劲，一边出汗一边笑。墙壁把我们困在一个不比沙发宽多少的空间里。最后表弟从底座下面钻了进去，我在前面拉，他在后面推，那东西才像头累坏了的牲口一样往上滑。还得把它硬拖过最后一道门，它才肯动。等它终于立在客厅里，我们坐在上面，谁也没说话。"},"wrinkle":{"tw":[["line",0],["pucker",3],["contract",2],["pill",6],["crisp",0],["fold",2],["nasal",6],["purse",0]],"en":"My grandmother reads the morning paper with a magnifying glass, and every year the lines around her eyes grow deeper. When she laughs, the skin at the corner of each eye puckers into a fine wrinkle that she calls her best feature. She takes one small pill after breakfast and complains that cold weather makes her voice nasal. In winter the skin on her hands contracts and folds into small dry creases, so she keeps a tin of cream by the sink. She purses her lips whenever she disagrees with the news, which is often. Her one wrinkle for stiff paper is to hold it near the kettle for a moment, until it turns crisp and easy to turn. She says age is a fair writer: it keeps a record on your face.","zh":"祖母看早报要用放大镜，眼角的纹路一年比一年深。她笑起来时，眼角那层皮会皱成一道细细的皱纹，她说那是她最好看的特征。早饭后她吃一小片药，还抱怨天冷的时候说话带鼻音。冬天她手上的皮肤会收紧，折出一道道干燥的褶子，所以水池边总放着一罐护手霜。她只要不赞同报上的消息就抿起嘴，而这样的情况很多。她对付硬报纸的妙招是把报纸在热水壶边放一会儿，等它变脆就好翻了。她说年纪是个公道的书记员：它把记录都写在你脸上。"},"salute":{"tw":[["drink",0],["fist",6],["present",0],["greet",2],["anthem",6],["toast",0]],"en":"On the last evening of his service, the crew gathered on the pier to salute the old ferry captain. A small band played the anthem badly but with feeling, and everyone stood still until the last note. Then the captain was asked to present the flag to the youngest sailor, which he did with both hands. One by one the others came to greet him, some shaking hands, some raising a fist to the chest in the old style. His mate lifted a glass and offered a toast that made the whole crowd laugh, and we all had a drink to the years he had crossed the water. I had expected a formal speech, but he only said that the tide never waits. We walked home slowly, and I could still hear the band.","zh":"在他工作的最后一晚，船员们聚在码头上向这位老渡船长行礼。小乐队把颂歌唱得并不好，却很有感情，大家一动不动站到最后一个音。然后有人请船长把旗子交给最年轻的水手，他双手递了过去。其他人一个个上前问候他，有的握手，有的按老规矩把拳头举到胸前。他的大副举起杯子说了段祝酒词，惹得全场大笑，我们也一起为他在水上奔波的那些年干了一杯。我本以为会有正式讲话，可他只说潮水从不等人。我们慢慢走回家，我耳边还响着乐队的声。"},"saturate":{"tw":[["impregnate",0],["charge",3],["change",2],["deflate",6],["stuff",3],["fill",2],["intoxicate",6]],"en":"In the lamp workshop, the first job of the morning was to saturate the new wicks with oil. We would stuff the cotton into a shallow tray, fill it to the brim, and leave it until every thread was dark. The oil would impregnate the fibres slowly, and a good wick held the flame without smoking. The old pump beside the bench had to charge the tank with air before we could test a burner, and when a seal failed the whole thing would deflate with a long sigh. The smell of the oil seemed to intoxicate the youngest apprentice; she stood there breathing it in until we called her. Nothing could change the routine: soak, wait, test. By noon the bench was crowded with lamps, and the room smelled of warm metal.","zh":"在灯具作坊里，早晨第一件事就是让新灯芯吸饱油。我们把棉花塞进浅盘，把油倒满，一直放到每根纤维都变深。油会慢慢浸透棉线，好的灯芯点起来不冒烟。工作台旁那台旧泵得先给罐子充气才能试灯头，密封圈一坏，整个东西就长长地泄气瘪下去。油的气味好像让最小的学徒有点醉了，她站在那儿一直闻，直到我们叫她。什么都改变不了这套流程：浸、等、试。到中午台面上摆满了灯，屋里全是热金属的味道。"},"scrub":{"tw":[["scratch",0],["wash",2],["bog",6],["cancel",0],["rub",2],["bark",6],["bush",0]],"en":"After the long walk across the moor, my boots were so covered in mud that I had to scrub them outside. The path had led us through a bog where the ground gave way at every step, and a low bush had left a deep scratch along my arm. I sat on the step with a bucket, a brush and an old cloth, and began to rub the wet earth out of the leather. It took an hour to wash the laces clean, and the bark of the tree above me kept dropping bits into the water. We had planned to walk again the next morning, but the weather report made us cancel. My sister said the whole trip had been a mistake, and I could only laugh and keep working.","zh":"在荒原上走了那一大圈之后，我的靴子沾满了泥，只好在门外刷。小路把我们带进一片沼泽，每走一步地面都往下陷，一丛矮灌木还在我胳膊上划了道深口子。我坐在台阶上，拿着水桶、刷子和一块旧布，开始把湿泥从皮革里搓出来。洗干净鞋带花了一个小时，头顶那棵树的树皮不停往水里掉渣。我们本来打算第二天再去走一趟，可天气预报让我们取消了。妹妹说这趟出门就是个错误，我只能笑着继续刷。"},"seam":{"tw":[["bed",0],["join",2],["wedge",6],["line",0],["joint",2],["pellet",6],["wrinkle",0]],"en":"The shoulder seam of my winter coat had opened, and the padding was coming out in small white clouds. I turned the coat inside out on the table and began to join the two edges with a line of small stitches. The joint was awkward, right where the sleeve meets the body, so I had to work slowly. I slipped a thin bed of new padding under the gap and pushed a wedge of cloth into the corner to keep the shape. Then I pressed a warm pellet of wax along the thread to make the seam watertight. When I turned the coat right side out, a wrinkle near the collar showed how uneven my work had been. It was not beautiful, but the coat was warm again.","zh":"我冬天外套的肩缝开了，填充物一小团一小团往外冒。我把外套翻过来摊在桌上，用一排小针脚把两边接上。接口正好在袖子和衣身相连的地方，很别扭，只能慢慢来。我在开口下垫了一层薄薄的新填充，又往角落里塞了一小块布撑住形状。然后我沿着线压上一粒温热的蜡，让缝口不漏水。把外套翻回正面时，领口附近的一道皱褶暴露出我缝得多不平整。不好看，但外套又暖和了。"},"shred":{"tw":[["tag",0],["tease",3],["tear",2],["extract",6],["rag",0],["discard",6],["tatter",0]],"en":"My mother spent Saturday sorting the bags of old clothes that had sat in the hall for months. Anything too worn to wear would go into the rag bag, and anything with a large hole would be cut into shreds for the workshop. She would tease apart the seams with her fingers, then tear the cloth along the grain so that nothing was wasted. One dress still had its price tag on, which made her stop and laugh. She tried to extract the receipt from the pocket, but it had turned to dust. The rest she would discard without regret, though a red tatter of silk went into her sewing box. By evening the hall was empty and the floor was pale with dust.","zh":"妈妈用星期六整理那些在门厅里放了好几个月的旧衣服袋子。太破不能穿的进抹布袋，破了大洞的就剪成碎布条送去做工坊的材料。她会用手指把缝线拆开，再顺着布纹撕开，一点都不浪费。有一条裙子还带着价签，她停下来笑了。她想把口袋里的收据抽出来，可它已经碎成粉末了。其余的她毫不心疼地丢掉，只有一片红色丝质碎布留进了针线盒。到傍晚门厅空了，地板上落着一层灰白。"},"shudder":{"tw":[["shiver",0],["fear",2],["wince",6],["chill",0],["tremble",2],["cringe",6],["thrill",0]],"en":"The waiting room was cold, and I could feel a chill coming up from the tiled floor. When the nurse called my name, a shudder ran through me that I could not hide. I have always had a fear of needles, and my hands began to tremble as I sat down. She told me to look away, and I did, but I still had to wince when the needle went in. For a second my whole body seemed to shiver, and then it was over. 'You did well,' she said, and I felt a small thrill of pride as I rolled my sleeve down. I used to cringe at the sight of a clinic, but this time I walked out almost cheerful.","zh":"候诊室很冷，我能觉出凉气从瓷砖地面往上冒。护士叫到我名字时，我忍不住打了个寒噤。我一直怕针，坐下时手就开始抖。她让我把头转开，我照做了，针扎进去时还是忍不住龇牙。有那么一秒钟我全身都在发抖，然后就结束了。她说“你做得不错”，我放下袖子时竟有点得意。以前我一看见诊所就发怵，这回走出去时心情几乎是轻松的。"},"singular":{"tw":[["odd",0],["form",2],["plural",1],["masculine",6],["peculiar",0],["characteristic",6]],"en":"In our grammar lesson the teacher wrote a sentence on the board and asked us to turn every singular noun into its plural form. Most of the class managed the first two words easily, but then she gave us an odd one: a noun that looks the same in both numbers. A boy said that the plural of that word was simply the same word again, which felt peculiar to the rest of us. She explained that this was a characteristic of a small group of nouns, and that the masculine ones often behave in the same way. Then she asked us to write a short paragraph using each form correctly. I filled half a page and was still not sure of the last line. Grammar, I decided, is full of quiet traps.","zh":"语法课上，老师在黑板上写了一个句子，让我们把每个单数名词都变成复数形式。大部分同学前两个词都很轻松，接着她给了一个奇怪的：一个单复数同形的名词。一个男生说那个词的复数就是它本身，我们其余人都觉得挺古怪。她解释说这是一小类名词的特点，而阳性名词往往也是这样。然后她让我们写一小段话，把每种形式都用对。我写了半页，最后一个句子还是没把握。我认定，语法里处处是安静的陷阱。"},"slack":{"tw":[["slow",0],["stretch",2],["rebound",6],["loose",0],["decrease",2],["bounce",6],["relax",0]],"en":"Business in the cafe always falls into a slack season in the weeks after the holiday, when the town empties and the orders decrease. The afternoons are slow, and there is time to relax behind the counter. Last Tuesday I finally fixed the loose rope of the awning, which would stretch in the wind and then rebound with a snap. A boy outside was bouncing a ball against the wall, and every bounce echoed in the empty room. I sat with a cup of tea and watched the street, waiting for a customer who never came. By five I had sold three coffees, and I decided to close early. Even a quiet season, I told myself, gives the chairs a rest.","zh":"假期过后的那几个星期，咖啡馆的生意总进入淡季，镇上空了，订单也减少。下午很慢，柜台后面有时间松口气。上周二我终于把遮阳篷那根松掉的绳子修好了，它原本一到风里就拉长，然后啪地弹回来。外面有个男孩一直往墙上拍球，每一下弹跳都在空店里回响。我端着一杯茶坐着看街，等一个始终没来的客人。到五点我只卖了三杯咖啡，就决定早点关门。我对自己说，就算是淡季，也让椅子歇一歇。"},"slaughter":{"tw":[["butcher",0],["kill",2],["cull",6],["massacre",0],["murder",2],["herd",6],["carnage",0]],"en":"The news that evening was about a disease that had spread through a herd of cattle on the plain. Farmers were told to cull the animals before it reached the next valley, and the slaughter began at dawn. A vet said the decision was necessary, but she admitted that the scene looked like carnage. The butcher in the village had worked there for thirty years, and he said he had never had to kill so many in one week. One farmer called it a massacre, and another said it felt like murder to load healthy animals onto the trucks. The report ended with a wide shot of empty fields. No one in the studio seemed to know what to say next.","zh":"那天晚上的新闻讲的是一种在平原牛群里蔓延的疾病。农民们被告知要在病情传到下一个山谷之前扑杀这些牛，屠宰在天亮时开始。一位兽医说这个决定是必要的，但她也承认那场面像一场血腥的屠戮。村里的屠夫在那儿干了三十年，他说自己从没在一个星期里杀过这么多。一个农民称之为屠杀，另一个说把健康的牛装上卡车感觉像谋杀。报道最后是一个空荡荡的田野远景。演播室里似乎没人知道接下来该说什么。"},"slick":{"tw":[["slip",0],["film",2],["rough",6],["pat",0],["polish",2],["splash",6],["glossy",0]],"en":"The kitchen floor was slick with oil from a pan I had dropped, and I nearly slipped twice before I found the cloth. A thin film of fat had spread across the tiles, catching the light and making the whole room look glossy. I knelt down and began to rub, first with a dry cloth, then with soap and hot water. My hands were rough from the cold, and every splash of water stung. When the floor was dry I gave it a quick polish and patted the wood at the edge with a towel. It looked better than it had in months, which was small comfort at eleven at night. I put the pan away and promised to be more careful.","zh":"厨房地面因为我打翻的一口锅而滑溜溜的，找到抹布之前我差点摔了两回。一层薄薄的油膜铺在瓷砖上，反着光，让整个屋子看着油亮亮的。我跪下来擦，先用干布，再用肥皂热水。我的手被冻得粗糙，每溅上一点水都刺痛。地干了我又快速抛了一遍光，用毛巾把边上的木条按干。它比这几个月里任何时候都干净，可这在夜里十一点算不上什么安慰。我把锅收好，向自己保证以后小心点。"},"sneak":{"tw":[["lift",0],["act",2],["shoot",6],["slip",0],["peek",6],["pass",2],["creep",0]],"en":"At two in the morning the cat began to sneak along the hallway towards the kitchen. She would creep past the bedroom door, stop, and then slip through the gap without a sound. From the sofa I watched her lift the lid of the fish pan with one paw. She would peek over the edge, then act as if she had found nothing at all. When I moved, she would shoot under the table and wait there, perfectly still. I took a photo of her eyes in the dark, then went back to bed and pretended to sleep. In the morning the pan was licked clean, and she passed me on the stairs without a look.","zh":"凌晨两点，猫开始沿着走廊偷偷往厨房去。她会悄悄经过卧室门口，停一下，然后无声地从门缝里溜进去。我坐在沙发上，看她用一只爪子掀起装鱼的锅盖。她探头往里看，接着装作什么都没发现。我一动，她就窜到桌子底下，一动不动地等着。我在黑里拍了一张她眼睛的照片，然后回床上装睡。早上锅被舔得干干净净，她在楼梯上从我身边走过，连看都没看我一眼。"},"sow":{"tw":[["seed",0],["broadcast",3],["circulate",2],["nip",6],["scatter",3],["swine",2]],"en":"On the small farm, the old sow had her own corner of the yard, and she ruled the other swine from it. In the next field my uncle would broadcast seed by hand, then scatter a little more where the ground was thin. He said the wind helped to circulate the seed through the rows, though it also carried some into the ditch. In April a late frost can nip the young plants, so he covered them with cloth at night. The sow watched all of this from behind the fence, her ears moving at every sound. When the first green showed, he let her out and she walked the rows as if she owned them. It was the quietest spring I have ever seen.","zh":"在小农场里，那头老母猪有自己的一块院子角落，还从那儿管着别的猪。旁边那块地里，叔叔会用手撒种，再在土薄的地方补撒一些。他说风能帮种子在垄间散开，不过也会把一些吹进水沟。四月里一场晚霜会把幼苗冻伤，所以他夜里给它们盖上布。母猪隔着篱笆看着这一切，耳朵随着每个声响转动。第一批绿芽冒出来时，他把她放出来，她走在垄间，好像那片地是她的。那是我见过最安静的春天。"},"spawn":{"tw":[["breed",0],["roe",3],["cause",2],["prey",6],["engender",0],["egg",2],["originate",6]],"en":"Every spring the frogs return to the pond behind the barn to breed, and by April the water is full of spawn. The roe lies in soft clouds among the weeds, each egg a small dark point inside a jelly case. Herons come for an easy meal, and the spawn is prey for fish and beetles as well. My father says the noise at night can cause a sleepless week, but he never complains for long. He likes to think the pond can engender new life out of nothing but rain and mud. Where the frogs originate is a mystery to me; one year there were none, the next there were hundreds. We sit on the bank and watch, saying nothing.","zh":"每年春天，青蛙都会回到谷仓后的池塘产卵，到四月水里满是蛙卵。卵在草丛间像一团团柔软的云，每颗蛋里都有一个深色的小点。苍鹭来捡现成的吃食，这些卵也是鱼和甲虫的猎物。父亲说夜里的叫声能让人一个星期睡不好，但他从不会抱怨太久。他愿意相信这池塘能只靠雨水和泥生出新的生命。这些青蛙是从哪儿来的，对我来说是个谜：有一年一只都没有，第二年就有几百只。我们坐在岸边看着，什么也不说。"},"spear":{"tw":[["shaft",0],["weapon",2],["claw",6],["gig",0],["implement",2],["dagger",6],["lance",0]],"en":"In the back room of the museum, an old man was repairing a fishing spear whose shaft had split. He held the wood against his knee, tested the balance, and then reached for a file. 'A gig like this,' he said, 'is not a weapon. It is a tool for eels, and a good one lasts a lifetime.' On the wall behind him hung a curved claw, a rusted dagger, and the long lance that had once belonged to a sailor. Every implement in that room had a story, and he knew them all. He showed me how the point was fixed with a wedge of bone, then wrapped the joint with cord. I left with the smell of oil in my clothes.","zh":"在博物馆的后屋里，一位老人正在修一支木柄裂了的鱼叉。他把木头抵在膝上试了试平衡，然后伸手去拿锉刀。他说：“这样的鱼叉不是武器，是叉鳗鱼的工具，好的能用一辈子。”他身后的墙上挂着一只弯爪、一把生锈的短剑，还有一支曾属于某个水手的长矛。那屋里每件器具都有来历，他全都知道。他给我看叉尖是怎么用一小块骨头固定的，然后用绳把接口缠好。我离开时衣服上都是油味。"},"sprout":{"tw":[["shoot",3],["bud",3],["grow",2],["wither",6],["stock",0],["prune",6],["germinate",0]],"en":"In March I planted a row of beans on the windowsill and waited for them to germinate. The first shoot appeared after nine days, a pale green hook pushing through the soil. Within a week each seed had become a small sprout with two flat leaves. I moved the pots to the brightest window, where they would grow straight instead of leaning. By May there were buds on the tallest plants, and I had to prune the lower leaves so the stock could put its strength into the fruit. One pot dried out while I was away, and its leaves began to wither. I watered it every morning after that, and it slowly came back.","zh":"三月我在窗台上种了一排豆子，等着它们发芽。第九天冒出第一根芽，像一只淡绿色的小钩子顶开泥土。一个星期之内，每颗种子都长成了一株带两片平叶的小苗。我把花盆挪到最亮的窗前，那里它们会直着长而不会歪。到五月最高的几株上有了花蕾，我只好剪掉下面的叶子，让主茎把力气都用在果实上。有一盆我不在时干透了，叶子开始枯萎。那以后我每天早上浇水，它慢慢缓了过来。"},"stray":{"tw":[["roll",0],["tell",2],["shoot",6],["cast",0],["travel",2],["explode",6],["range",0]],"en":"A thin brown stray had been sleeping behind the bins for a week before anyone spoke to it. You could tell it had travelled a long way, because its paws were cut and its coat was full of burrs. In the daytime it would range along the back lanes, and at dusk it came back to the same corner. The first time I offered it bread, it would roll over and show its belly, then shoot away if I moved. I sat still and cast a quick look at the gate to see if anyone owned it. When a car backfired, the dog seemed to explode into the hedge and was gone. It came back the next night, and the night after that.","zh":"一只瘦瘦的棕色流浪狗在垃圾桶后面睡了一个星期，才有人跟它说话。看得出它走了很远的路，爪子破了，毛里全是草刺。白天它沿着后巷四处游荡，天黑就回到同一个角落。我第一次给它面包时，它翻过身露出肚子，我一动就窜开了。我坐着不动，飞快地朝大门瞥了一眼，看是不是有主人。一辆车回火时，它像炸开一样冲进树篱不见了。第二天晚上它又回来了，再下一晚也是。"},"substantive":{"tw":[["essential",5],["noun",3],["word",2],["adjective",1],["formal",6],["substantial",0],["compromise",6]],"en":"Our writing teacher returned the reports with a single note in the margin: make a substantive change, not a cosmetic one. Most of us had only replaced a noun with an adjective and called it editing. She said that a formal style is not the same as a good argument, and that a long word is not always the essential one. A substantial part of the mark, she explained, came from evidence rather than vocabulary. We were allowed one compromise: we could keep our opening sentence if we could defend it. I spent the evening rewriting my second paragraph and cutting two pages. The next draft was shorter, plainer, and much better.","zh":"写作老师把报告发回来，页边只有一句批注：要做实质性的修改，不是表面功夫。我们大多数人只是把一个名词换成了形容词，就叫它修改了。她说正式的文风不等于好的论证，长词也不一定就是最关键的那个。她解释说，分数里有相当大一部分来自证据，而不是词汇。她允许我们做一个让步：只要能说清理由，开头那句可以保留。我花了一晚上重写第二段，删了两页。下一稿更短、更朴素，也好得多。"},"swirl":{"tw":[["whirl",0],["run",2],["stir",6],["twirl",0],["revolve",2],["mist",6],["eddy",0]],"en":"By six the mist had come down over the river, and the water below the bridge turned in a slow swirl around the stone. A thin eddy circled beside the bank, carrying leaves round and round, and the whole surface seemed to revolve without moving forward. My father stood at the tiller and let the engine run at half speed, watching the fog rather than the shore. Every few minutes a gust would stir the mist into a whirl and then let it settle again. A heron rose from the reeds and began to twirl upward until it vanished. We said nothing; the river was making all the noise there was. Then the sun broke through, and the world came back.","zh":"六点前雾落到了河面上，桥下的水绕着石头转成一个缓慢的漩涡。岸边有个细小的涡流打着圈，把落叶一圈圈带走，整个水面像在旋转却不向前。父亲站在舵旁，让发动机半速运转，眼睛盯着雾而不是岸。每隔几分钟就有一阵风把雾搅成一个旋涡，然后又让它沉下来。一只苍鹭从芦苇里飞起，盘旋着向上，直到看不见。我们都没说话，所有的声音都是河水发出的。后来太阳透出来，世界又回来了。"},"tame":{"tw":[["moderate",0],["change",2],["wild",1],["bounce",6],["cultivate",0],["adapt",2],["reclaim",0]],"en":"The colt came to us wild, and for the first month he would not let anyone within ten feet. My aunt would sit in the field for hours, talking quietly, until the horse began to adapt to her voice. It took a year to tame him, and even now he will bounce sideways if a bag flaps in the wind. She says a horse does not change its nature, only its habits. Beyond the fence, the family has started to reclaim an old orchard and cultivate the ground again, with moderate success. The soil is poor, and every season brings a new problem. Still, the apples are better than anything we buy.","zh":"那匹小马到我们家时是野的，头一个月谁都不能靠近十英尺以内。姑姑会在田里坐上几个小时，轻声说话，直到它开始适应她的声音。把它驯服花了一年，就算现在，只要有袋子在风里扑动，它还会往旁边一蹦。她说马改变不了本性，只能改变习惯。篱笆外面，家里人开始重新开垦一片老果园，又把地种起来，收成还算过得去。土很贫，每一季都有新麻烦。不过那些苹果比我们买来的都好吃。"},"tan":{"tw":[["burn",0],["bark",3],["convert",2],["bronze",0],["wan",6]],"en":"In the leather workshop, the hides are first treated with a tan made from oak bark, which gives them their deep brown colour. The process is slow: the skin must sit in the liquid for weeks before it will convert into soft, workable leather. A careless hand can burn the surface, and then the whole piece is spoiled. The old craftsman showed me a belt that had aged into a warm bronze shade, almost like the tan of a summer arm. His own face was pale and wan from years indoors, but his eyes were sharp. He said the work teaches patience, and that a hurried piece always shows. I left with a small notebook cover, still smelling of the bath.","zh":"在皮革作坊里，皮子先要用橡树皮做的鞣料处理，那会给它们深褐的颜色。过程很慢：皮得在液体里泡上几个星期，才会变成柔软好用的革。手一不留意就会把表面烧坏，那一整块就废了。老匠人给我看一条皮带，已经养出温润的青铜色，几乎像夏天手臂晒出的黄褐色。他自己的脸因为常年待在室内而苍白憔悴，眼睛却很利。他说这活儿教人耐心，赶工的活儿总看得出来。我走的时候带着一个笔记本封皮，还留着鞣池的味道。"},"toll":{"tw":[["cost",0],["ring",2],["surge",6],["price",0],["sound",2],["flood",6],["bell",0]],"en":"We left before dawn, because the toll road becomes a slow river of cars once the holiday traffic begins to surge. The cost of the crossing had gone up again, and my uncle complained about the price for the first twenty miles. Then rain closed the valley road, and a flood forced us onto a detour through the hills. At a small chapel we stopped to stretch our legs, and the bell began to ring for the morning service. The sound carried a long way in the wet air. My uncle said the trip was costing him more than a flight, but he was smiling. We reached the coast by noon.","zh":"我们天亮前就出发了，因为一到假期车流涌上来，那条收费公路就成了一条缓慢的车河。过路的费用又涨了，叔叔为这个价钱抱怨了头二十英里。后来下雨封了山谷里的路，一场洪水把我们逼上了绕山的路。在一座小教堂旁我们停下来活动腿脚，钟开始为晨祷敲响。声音在潮湿的空气里传得很远。叔叔说这趟路费比坐飞机还贵，可他一直笑着。中午我们到了海边。"},"tread":{"tw":[["step",2],["travel",2],["ruffle",6],["pace",0],["walk",2],["fret",6],["stride",0]],"en":"The tread of my boots had worn smooth, so every wet stone on the path felt dangerous. We had travelled for two days and the map showed another ridge before the village. My sister set a steady pace, and I tried to match her stride without saying that my knee hurt. A cold wind would ruffle the grass on the slope, then drop again into silence. We stopped to rest where a stream crossed the path, and I took off one boot to check the sole. 'Do not fret about the time,' she said. 'We walk until we are there.' The last step into the square was the easiest of the day.","zh":"我靴子的鞋底已经磨平了，路上每块湿石头都让人觉得危险。我们已经走了两天，地图上显示到村子之前还有一道山脊。姐姐保持着稳定的速度，我努力跟上她的步子，没说自己膝盖疼。冷风会把坡上的草吹得起伏，然后又静下来。我们在小溪横过小路的地方停下来歇脚，我脱下一只靴子看鞋底。她说：“别为时间发愁，走到就到了。”踏进广场的那一步是那天最轻松的。"},"vacuum":{"tw":[["void",0],["clean",2],["thermal",6],["vacancy",0],["space",2],["fluid",6],["hoover",3]],"en":"In the science club we spent a whole afternoon testing what a vacuum does to sound and heat. The teacher put a small bell inside a glass jar, sealed it, and pumped the air out until the space inside was almost empty. In that void the bell could still be seen ringing, but we heard nothing at all. She explained that without a fluid such as air, sound has nothing to travel through. Then she showed us a thermal flask, whose double wall slows the loss of heat. One boy asked whether the vacancy inside a sealed jar could ever be truly complete. Nobody could answer, so we cleaned up and put the hoover away.","zh":"在科学小组里，我们花了一整个下午测试真空对声音和热的影响。老师把一只小铃放进玻璃罐，封好，把空气抽出去，直到里面的空间几乎空了。在那片真空里，看得见铃在响，我们却一点声音也听不到。她解释说，没有空气这样的流体，声音就没有东西可以传播。然后她给我们看了一个保温瓶，双层壁能减慢热的散失。一个男生问，密封罐里的那片空缺能不能真正做到完全空。没人答得上来，于是我们收拾干净，把吸尘器收起来。"},"vent":{"tw":[["air",0],["express",2],["exhaust",6],["release",0],["hole",2],["spout",6],["outlet",0]],"en":"On Monday the office smelled of old coffee, because the vent above the kitchen had been blocked for a week. Someone had pushed a box against the outlet, and the warm air had nowhere to go. The maintenance man climbed a ladder, found a small hole in the duct, and taped it shut. He said the exhaust from the printer was part of the problem, and that the room needed a proper spout to carry it away. By lunchtime we could feel the air moving again. My manager used the chance to express her thanks with a box of cakes. It was a small release of tension, but everyone was grateful.","zh":"星期一办公室里有股陈咖啡味，因为厨房上方的通风口已经堵了一个星期。有人把箱子推到了出风口前面，暖空气无处可去。维修工爬上梯子，发现管道上有个小洞，就用胶带封住了。他说打印机排出的废气也是一部分原因，这屋子需要一个像样的排风管把它带走。到午饭时我们已经能感觉到空气在动了。经理借这个机会用一盒蛋糕表达了谢意。那只是一点小小的放松，但大家都很感激。"},"voyage":{"tw":[["sail",0],["cruise",3],["travel",2],["ship",6],["navigate",0],["journey",2],["excursion",6]],"en":"The voyage across the channel took three days, and for the first two the ship moved through a grey, flat sea with no land in sight. We had chosen a slow crossing rather than a cruise, because my grandfather wanted time to watch the water. He would stand at the rail for hours and try to navigate by the shape of the clouds. In the evenings he told us about his first journey, made when he was nineteen and had never travelled beyond his own valley. On the last morning the captain let us sail a small boat around the bay as an excursion. My grandfather took the tiller and laughed like a boy.","zh":"横渡海峡的航行用了三天，头两天船在灰而平的海面上行驶。我们选的是一趟慢船，而不是游轮，因为祖父想有时间看海。他会在栏杆旁站上几个小时，试着凭云的形状判断方向。晚上他给我们讲他第一次出远门的事，那时他十九岁，从没离开过自己那个山谷。最后一天早上，船长让我们驾一条小船绕海湾一圈，当作短途游览。祖父握住舵柄，笑得像个孩子。"},"wail":{"tw":[["roar",0],["cry",2],["plaintive",6],["howl",0],["shout",2],["mournful",6],["lament",0]],"en":"At midnight the wind began to roar around the windows, and then came a sound that was almost human. It would howl for a minute, drop, and rise again in a long, mournful wail. My daughter had a fever, and she began to cry in her sleep, a thin and plaintive sound that made me stand up at once. I carried her to the kitchen and held a cup of water to her lips. She did not shout or complain about the heat; she only leaned against me and went quiet. Outside, the storm seemed to lament the whole night through. By morning the fever had gone, and the wind with it, and the house was quiet again.","zh":"午夜时风开始绕着窗户呼啸，接着传来一个几乎像人的声音。它会嚎上一分钟，低下去，然后又拖成一声长长的哀号。女儿在发烧，睡梦里哭了起来，那声音又细又哀，我立刻站了起来。我把她抱到厨房，把一杯水送到她嘴边。她没有喊也没有闹，只是靠在我身上安静下来。窗外，暴风雨像是在哀悼，整夜不停。到早上烧退了，风也停了。"}}});
